 A hundred and ninety DISTINCT corpus words. What this input is for is not the
 dictionary but the CODE-LENGTH REPAIR underneath it: many distinct words give
 many distinct insert-and-copy symbols, and a description over about twenty of
 them is what used to defeat the repair.

 The repair lengthened the shortest code until the Kraft sum was no longer
 OVER-subscribed and stopped there. Each step changes the sum by a power of two,
 so it could step past equality and leave the code UNDER-subscribed -- incomplete,
 rejected by its own space check, the plan discarded as brotli-huge with no
 diagnostic. Aiming at equality instead takes this input from 594 bytes to 545.

 THE PIN IS ON THE SIZE, NOT ON THE ROUND-TRIP, and it has to be: the round-trip
 passed the whole time. A discarded plan is not a wrong answer, it is a silently
 worse one, so only a size can see it.

