 Corpus words each followed by one of the dictionary's own phrase suffixes --
 " of the ", " and ", ", " -- which is what the word transforms exist for. A
 transform is a word plus an affix, so an input where those affixes actually
 occur is the only place the search can pay.

 THE THRESHOLD SITS BETWEEN TWO MEASURED NUMBERS: 573 bytes with the transform
 plan costed out of the running, 562 with it in. The gain is two per cent, which
 is small and which is the point -- a transformed word carries a much larger id
 and so a more expensive distance, so it wins narrowly where the affix is real
 and loses everywhere else. The plan is costed against the same plan without
 transforms, so losing means it is simply not chosen.

